@@ -81,6 +82,8 @@ ## Discord ops alerts
 );
 ```
 
+When `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` is set to a valid Discord user ID (a snowflake: 17–20 digits, e.g., `123456789012345678`), every alert ends with a mention on its own line (`<@USER_ID>`). The mention consumes space within the 1800-character limit, so very long alerts truncate the title/message/context to preserve the mention. Invalid IDs (too short, non-numeric, `@everyone`, etc.) are silently ignored.
+
 ## VPS target
 
 - VM **700899** (`103.199.186.228`), Ubuntu + Docker
